[- XML-style structured document with xmlns namespace declarations.
   Demonstrates the namespace bearer pattern (ADR 0002): xmlns: as an
   inherited attribute scoped to the declaring element and descendants. ]

[chapter id=getting-started lang=en xmlns=https://cxhome.org/ns/doc xmlns:dc=http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/
  [title Getting Started with CX]
  [meta
    [- prefixed names resolve to the http://purl.org/dc URI at parse time ]
    [dc:author Erik Paulson]
    [dc:date 2026-04-20]
    [dc:identifier urn:cx:chapter:getting-started]
    [version :string 1.0]                # forced :string so 1.0 stays "1.0", not float 1
    [keywords :string[] cx format tutorial getting-started]
  ]

  [abstract
    [p CX is a compact, typed format for configs, data, and documents —
       all in one unified bracket syntax.]
    [p This chapter introduces the core concepts and shows how a single
       CX source converts to XML, JSON, YAML, TOML, and Markdown.]
  ]

  [section id=elements
    [title Elements and Attributes]
    [p An [em element] is a named bracket. Attributes carry typed scalars —
       no schema or quotes required:]
    [listing lang=cx [# [server host=localhost :u16 port=8080 +tls] #]]
    [p CX infers types automatically — and v3.4 sized types pin the width:]
    [- typed table: every type column is a real CX type token ]
    [examples :table[value:string inferred:string sized:string]
      '8080'         'int'    ':u16 → 0..65535'
      '3.14'         'float'  ':f32 / :f64'
      'true'         'bool'   '+flag / -flag sigils'
      '2026-04-20'   'date'   ':d alias'
      'null'         'null'   '— (no sized form)'
      '02134'        'string' '— (leading-zero stays string in v3.4)'
      '1_000_000'    'int'    ':u32 1_000_000 (underscore separator)'
    ]
  ]

  [section id=nesting
    [title Nesting and Mixed Content]
    [p Elements nest freely. Text and child elements mix in the same container:]
    [listing lang=cx [#
[article
  [head [title My Report] [author J. Smith]]
  [body
    [h1 Overview]
    [p This report covers [em three] key findings.]
  ]
]
    #]]
    [note type=tip
      [p CX round-trips cleanly: parsing and re-emitting produces
         normalised, diff-friendly output.]
    ]
  ]

  [section id=formats
    [title Output Formats]
    [p One source file, any target format. The [code cx] CLI and
       [code libcx] library support nine language bindings plus the
       native V reference implementation:]
    [ul
      [li [code cx --xml   chapter.cx] — DocBook-style XML]
      [li [code cx --json  chapter.cx] — API-ready JSON]
      [li [code cx --yaml  chapter.cx] — YAML for editors]
      [li [code cx --toml  chapter.cx] — TOML for configs]
      [li [code cx --md    chapter.cx] — Markdown for docs]
    ]
  ]
]
